id: pm-memory-sdk-host-alignment-1122
title: Adopt pm-cli 2026.11.27 host-aligned SDK behaviour
description: "Update the exact-pinned pm-memory toolchain and adopt the native host mutation guard contract introduced by GH-1719 and GH-1729. Verify the published compact JSON scanner fix and stabilize the orphaned slot claimer regression tracked by pm-memory-github-f33c4a70a040-98. Companion item: pm-cli-website-spus."
type: Chore
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags[2]: deps,sdk
created_at: "2026-11-23T09:58:32.707Z"
updated_at: "2026-11-27T11:37:33.940Z"
author: codex-agent
acceptance_criteria: Pin all first-party tooling to npm latest and refresh the committed lockfile.; Use host actor and dry-run context at guard boundaries and preserve fail-closed behaviour.; Pass the package release gates at unchanged coverage thresholds and regenerate the changelog.; Open a dedicated PR with failure classifications and verification evidence.
comments[9]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-23T14:31:38.088Z",codex-agent,"## SDK migration\n\n- `TS2345` in `src/native-host.ts` and `actual CLI origin refusals retain structured codes and create remedies without retargeting aliases`. The old discovery call supplied snapshots alone. The SDK now resolves an actor from the supplied author and distinguishes previews from writes. Discovery supplies the effective author and `dry_run: true`. The locked revision guard receives the SDK's real write context.\n- `portable host update publishes through the attested SDK guard`. The old preview inherited the injected client's fallback author, and SDK previews skipped mutation guards. The new preview evaluates guards on the staged tracker. Preview and publication now use the portable plan author, and the tests verify the phases and preserve refusal of foreign writes.\n- `TS2339` on portable mutation options. The SDK's bulk union gained `finalize`. Portable plans now use its create/update subset, matching the persisted plan validator.\n- `host publication fails closed without an in-process revision guard: foreign-missing-item`, `cross-process exact ownership at every create boundary`, `forward-only update: seeded peer operations at every import boundary`, `recovery and fresh CAS refuse newer remember edits at every journal boundary`, and `locked SDK revision refuses a concurrent foreign-field edit (host)`. Nested calls can no longer switch `cwd` or inherit hooks through a new `noExtensions` client. Fixture operations use a tracker path, foreign initialization happens outside the caller's scope, and the independent writer explicitly binds its oracle to its own active scope. [pm-cli 2026.11.23 SDK contract](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/releases/tag/v2026.11.23)\n- `standalone registration reads command context once and retains every schema boundary`. The old nested client reused its caller's scope implicitly. The newer SDK ran 28 context reads. A fenced client bound to the single extension-free scope restores the one-read assertion.\n- `complete SDK positives cannot be masked by a safe reference or a later local finding`, `reference boundaries inspect adjacent quoted literals and preserve pure reference twins`, and `reference terminators inspect 100000 spaces within a bounded process deadline`. The SDK accepts a complete bare environment reference and measures literal continuations, including annotations inside quoted passwords and assignment text glued to a prior value. The tests exercise separated references and attached literals under that contract. [SDK scanner behavior](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/pull/1745), [reference handling](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/pull/1746)\n\nExact development pins are `@unbrained/pm-cli` 2026.11.23, `pm-changelog` 2026.11.20 and `pm-ops` 2026.11.22. The peer and manifest floor follow the reviewed host.\n\n## Upstream blockers\n\n`compound credential control 5 remains writable and portable` and the valid-reference round trip fail because the SDK scans across string boundaries in compact JSON. `quoted scanner preserves the prior matcher corpus` also fails at full depth on an escape-only value. Both reproduce with the public SDK alone.\n\n```js\nimport { scanMutationSecrets } from '@unbrained/pm-cli/sdk'\n\nconst compact = JSON.stringify({\n  title: 'api_key: ${API_KEY}',\n  updated: '2026-11-23T00:00:00.000Z',\n})\nconst quote = String.fromCharCode(39)\nconst escapeOnly = `${quote}password${quote}: ${quote}${String.fromCharCode(92).repeat(7)}${quote}`\nfor (const input of [compact, escapeOnly]) {\n  console.log(scanMutationSecrets(input).map(({ rule }) => rule))\n}\n```\n\n2026.11.14 returns `[]` for both inputs. 2026.11.23 reports `credential_key_assignment` and `password_assignment`, respectively.\n\n## Verification\n\n- Initial `npm run release:check` on the earlier migration iteration ran 934 tests (919 pass, 15 fail). The diagnostic coverage snapshot was 99.98% statements, 99.67% branches, 100% functions and 99.98% lines.\n- `bun install --no-save` succeeded from the committed npm lock. `bun run release:check` on the rebased code reached 425 passes, one scanner failure and two file watchdogs before switching to the scope fallback at 110 minutes. The interrupted report counted 52 cancellations.\n- Direct fallback with `PM_TEST_DEPTH=quick` and two single-worker lanes recorded 236/236 SDK and CLI cases, 268/269 portable and review cases, 26/26 preview and publication cases, and 7/7 unfinished forward cases. The one failure is the valid-reference compact JSON round trip.\n- The import-state and lossless export watchdogs passed under the slow-host Bun retry. The direct model retry passed 50 seeds and 2,290 SDK-read steps. Every forward case completed across the Bun run and its direct retry.\n- Focused migration tests passed 74/74. The linked `pm test --run --progress` command passed 25/25. Each individual source revert failed its author, preview or registration assertion, and the three controls passed after restoring the source.\n- Packed npm and Bun consumer tests passed 4/4. Build, typecheck, lint, identity, 0% duplication, docstrings, production audit (zero vulnerabilities), release attestation, isolated tracker health and validation, and the changelog check passed.\n- The configured 100% coverage gate remains blocked. The full-depth quoted corpus check independently reproduced the escape-only SDK finding.\n\nTracker: [pm-memory-sdk-host-alignment-1122](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-memory/blob/main/.agents/pm/chores/pm-memory-sdk-host-alignment-1122.toon)"
  "2026-11-25T05:57:17.500Z",codex-agent,"Continuing the existing migration on the published host fix. Merge main, refresh the exact toolchain and changelog, then verify the compact JSON controls and add a bounded parent-death test with a behavioral revert and Node 26 repetitions."
  "2026-11-25T06:05:10.988Z",codex-agent,"The published 2026.11.25 SDK accepts the bare and compact API-key reference and still flags a synthetic literal. The compound credential control now passes. The separate annotation round trip still fails before the imported-count equality at test/reference-suffix.test.ts:119. The same single-quoted password reference is accepted standalone and in pretty JSON but gives password_assignment as a compact JSON title followed by an updated field. The full-depth quoted digest also differs because the published scanner still finds password_assignment on an escape-only input. Version 2026.11.14 reports no finding on either synthetic input. The existing tests and complete-value privacy checks remain in force."
  "2026-11-25T06:07:21.163Z",codex-agent,"Node 26.13.0 with two file slots: orphan test passed 50/50 baseline and 50/50 with one busy CPU pinned to the same core as the test. Revert proof in a disposable copy: changing only the fixture loop to ignore parent death failed at an orphaned claimer must stop instead of spinning; the original fixture passed 1/1 afterward. Linked pm test ran all four registered files, 82 passed and one failed at the known compact single-quoted reference import. Changelog entry-point test passed."
  "2026-11-25T06:34:11.282Z",codex-agent,"Node 26.13.0 quick depth, two file slots, scaled deadlines: 55 scoped files ran 742 cases with 741 passes and one upstream compact single-quoted reference failure. The four additional README and privacy files passed 29/29, for 770/771 total across 59 files, with zero skips or cancellations. The independent full-depth quoted corpus assertion failed 0/1 as classified above. Build, typecheck, lint, 0% duplication, docstrings, identity, isolated tracker health and validation passed. The npm lock pins the published host. A scratch Bun lock generated from the npm lock installed the same published versions with the repo's no-save graph smoke. PR CI owns the quick Node 22 and Node 26 gates, including the unchanged 100% coverage requirements on Node 26. The existing main-branch CI Deep workflow owns the full npm and Bun gates. PR checks: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-memory/pull/96/checks.\n\nMinimal public SDK reproduction for the remaining compact scanner case: set q to String.fromCharCode(39) and ref to String.fromCharCode(36, 123) + 'BUILD_PASSWORD}'. Set title to q + 'password' + q + String.fromCharCode(58, 32) + q + ref + q. Scan JSON.stringify({ title, updated }) with updated set to an ISO timestamp. The published host reports password_assignment for the compact form and no finding when JSON.stringify uses indentation. For the separate full-depth case, use q + 'password' + q + String.fromCharCode(58, 32) + q + String.fromCharCode(92).repeat(7) + q."
  "2026-11-27T10:46:28.073Z",codex-agent,"Resume the SDK migration with the published pm-cli 2026.11.27 scanner fix. Verify the unchanged compact reference transfer and full-depth verdict digest, keep literal credential refusals, refresh the npm and Bun dependency graphs, and hand off the coverage and release gates to exact-head CI."
  "2026-11-27T10:48:35.791Z",codex-agent,"With the old 2026.11.25 host, the unchanged selected tests failed 0/2: the annotation transfer raised privacy before the import count at test/reference-suffix.test.ts:119, and the full-depth digest differed at test/sdk-review-r8.test.ts:42. On the published 2026.11.27 host both passed, 2/2. The peer floor follows the host fix because the annotation transfer is supported behavior. No package workaround or assertion change was needed."
  "2026-11-27T10:49:36.877Z",codex-agent,"The lock refresh changes only the three first-party tool pins. npm ci passed. Bun generated a 208-entry scratch lock from the tracked npm lock, then installed 181 packages with the frozen lock and confirmed the same three pins. The production audit reported zero vulnerabilities. The unchanged dev-only c8 advisory is tracked in pm-memory-c8-glob-advisory."
  "2026-11-27T11:37:32.605Z",codex-agent,"Node 26.13.0 with two file workers and scaled deadlines passed all 353 quick cases across 27 files referencing this continuation's changed package metadata or docs and covering privacy and the orphan regression. There were zero failures, cancellations, skips or todos. The packed-documentation assertion passed 1/1. The linked pm test command repeated the two full-depth regressions and passed 2/2. Four published SDK scanner controls passed. Build, test build, typecheck, lint, duplication at 0 percent, docstrings for 249 declarations, release attestation, strict tracker health and tracker validation passed. Exact-head CI owns the coverage and full release gates and its run is linked from https://github.com/unbraind/pm-memory/pull/96/checks. The draft becomes ready only after the pushed head's CI passes."
